  "id": "Compound::DB00763 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Methimazole appears to interact with Cyp2c19 through a shared pathway involving arachidonic acid metabolism. The evidence suggests that Methimazole binds to Cyp2a6, which then participates in the oxidation of arachidonic acid, a process catalyzed by Cyp2c19. This indicates a potential mechanism where Methimazole may influence Cyp2c19's activity by modulating the expression or function of Cyp2a6, which in turn affects arachidonic acid metabolism. The overlapping roles of Cyp2a6 and Cyp2c19 in arachidonic acid metabolism suggest a possible functional link between these enzymes, possibly through shared regulatory mechanisms or co-expression in certain tissues. The consistent scores across the three paths support a robust relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
